---
import Bot from './Bot.astro';import '../styles/blocks.css';
const {lesson,free=false}=Astro.props;
---
<section class="block-lab" data-lesson={lesson?.slug||'free'} aria-label="Visual coding playground">
<div class="block-topbar"><span class="pill">▦ BLOCK LAB <span class="block-beta-label">· made for making</span></span><div class="block-actions"><button class="button small dark" id="blocks-run" disabled>▶ Run my blocks</button><button class="button small white" id="blocks-stop" disabled>■ Stop</button>{!free&&<button class="button small" id="blocks-check" disabled>✓ Check my task</button>}</div></div>
<div class="block-instructions"><p><strong>Build it:</strong> choose a toolbox category, drag blocks onto the canvas, then snap instructions inside <b>when I press Run</b>. Drop values into matching sockets. Edit words or numbers directly on their blocks.</p><label for="blocks-speed">Watch it happen <select id="blocks-speed"><option value="90">Slow & steady</option><option value="20">Quick</option><option value="0">Instant</option></select></label></div>
<div class="block-grid"><div class="workspace-column"><div id="blockly-workspace" aria-label="Block editor canvas"><p class="block-loading">Waking up the blocks…</p></div><div class="workspace-tools"><button class="tool-btn" id="blocks-undo" disabled>↶ Undo</button><button class="tool-btn" id="blocks-redo" disabled>↷ Redo</button><button class="tool-btn" id="blocks-fit" disabled>Fit blocks</button><button class="tool-btn" id="blocks-reset" disabled>Start over</button><button class="tool-btn" id="blocks-save" disabled>Download project ↓</button><label class="tool-btn file-label">Open project <input type="file" id="blocks-open" accept=".json,application/json" disabled/></label></div><p class="tiny" id="blocks-save-status">Projects are saved on this device when storage is available.</p></div><aside class="block-stage"><div class="stage-scene"><span class="stage-spark s1">✦</span><span class="stage-spark s2">+</span><div class="bit-bubble" id="bit-speech">Let’s make something happen!</div><Bot size={125}/><span class="stage-ground"></span></div><div class="stage-output"><h3>Bit’s messages</h3><pre id="blocks-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Program output">Your messages will appear here.</pre></div><details open class="variable-panel"><summary>What’s in your variables?</summary><div id="blocks-variables"><p class="tiny">Set a variable to see its name, value, and type here.</p></div></details></aside></div>
<div class="block-status" id="blocks-status" role="status">Loading the visual editor…</div>
<div class="block-bottom"><details class="block-inputs" open={!!lesson?.inputs?.length}><summary>Inputs <span>Try different values</span></summary><p class="tiny">Inputs give your program information. An “input” block reads a value by its exact name. Task checks use their own values.</p><div id="blocks-input-fields"></div>{free&&<div class="input-add"><label>Name <input id="new-input-name" type="text" maxlength="30" placeholder="friends"/></label><label>Type <select id="new-input-type"><option value="number">Number</option><option value="text">Text</option><option value="boolean">Boolean</option></select></label><button class="button small ghost" id="add-block-input">Add input</button></div>}</details><details class="block-python"><summary>From blocks to Python <span>A bridge to your next adventure</span></summary><p class="tiny">Generate real Python from these blocks. The helper functions keep Bit’s messages familiar. Python has its own type rules; the <a href="/python/">Python trail</a> explains them.</p><button class="button small ghost" id="blocks-python" disabled>Show the Python</button><button class="button small dark" id="blocks-to-python" disabled>Open in Python playground ↗</button><pre id="blocks-python-code"></pre></details></div>
<noscript><p class="feedback">Turn on JavaScript to use the block editor. You can still read every lesson and its hints.</p></noscript>
</section>
<dialog id="blocks-confirm"><h2 id="blocks-confirm-title">Start a fresh plan?</h2><p id="blocks-confirm-description">This replaces the blocks on this canvas. Download your project first if you want to keep a copy.</p><div class="actions"><button class="button" id="blocks-confirm-yes">Replace blocks</button><form method="dialog"><button class="button ghost">Keep my blocks</button></form></div></dialog>
<script>import '../scripts/blocks';</script>
